## Install

{% if registry %}If this plugin has a published release in the
[MemCastle plugin catalogue](https://memcastle.github.io/plugins.json),
install it by ID with a plugin-capable MemCastle Core binary:

```sh
memcastle plugin install {{ plugin_id }}
```

Core retrieves and checks the release archive for you.

If the catalogue entry has no published release yet, build and package the project first (below).
{% else %}Get the `{{ plugin_id }}-VERSION.tar.gz` archive from this repository's
[Releases](https://github.com/{{ github_owner }}/{{ repository_name }}/releases).
With a plugin-capable MemCastle Core binary, install the downloaded archive:

```sh
memcastle plugin install ./{{ plugin_id }}-VERSION.tar.gz
```

Replace `VERSION` with the downloaded release version.

The archive is the installation unit; you don't need to fetch its modules separately.
{% endif %}{% if sources %}
After installation, explicitly enable the sources you want to use.
{% endif %}{% if integrations %}
Register integrations with your agent separately; installing the archive alone does not configure an agent.
{% endif %}{% if embeddings %}
Select an embedding provider through a named embedding connection after installing the plugin.
{% endif %}
{% if sources or embeddings %}
Source and embedding components require migrated development Core from commit `828f0f6` or a descendant
(Wasmtime 50.0.3).
Stable 0.5.2 predates this migration even though development currently reports the same version.
The default `>=0.5, <0.6` compatibility range is transitional; tighten it when a compatible stable release exists.
{% endif %}
## Build and test locally

You'll need a plugin-capable MemCastle Core binary and Git.
{% if sources or embeddings %}
Install Rust 1.100+ with `rustup target add wasm32-wasip3`, wasm-tools 1.263.0, and Python 3.11+.
These components use WASI 0.3.0, source contract 0.5.0 and embedding contract 0.2.0.
WASI 0.3 support is experimental and does not enable `std::thread::spawn`.
An external WASI SDK is only needed for builds that explicitly depend on it.
{% endif %}{% if integrations %}Install Bun for agent integrations.
{% endif %}
{% if sources %}For each source, run its tests, build the Wasm component and copy the compiled component
to `sources/<id>/source.wasm`.
See the module's README and the CI workflow for its crate-specific artifact name:

```sh
cargo generate-lockfile --manifest-path sources/<id>/Cargo.toml
cargo test --manifest-path sources/<id>/Cargo.toml --locked --lib
cargo build --manifest-path sources/<id>/Cargo.toml --locked --release --target wasm32-wasip3
```

{% endif %}{% if embeddings %}For each embedding provider, run its native tests and build its component
to `embeddings/<id>/embedding.wasm`:

```sh
cargo generate-lockfile --manifest-path embeddings/<id>/Cargo.toml
cargo test --manifest-path embeddings/<id>/Cargo.toml --locked --lib
cargo build --manifest-path embeddings/<id>/Cargo.toml --locked --release --target wasm32-wasip3
```

{% endif %}{% if integrations %}For each integration with a `package.json`,
install dependencies, test and build in its directory:

```sh
cd integrations/<id>
bun install
bun test --timeout 60000
bun run build
cd ../..
```

{% endif %}From the project root, package and smoke-test the result:

```sh
memcastle plugin inspect --json
memcastle plugin package
memcastle plugin test dist/{{ plugin_id }}-VERSION.tar.gz
```

Replace `VERSION` with the version printed by `memcastle plugin package`
or the name of the archive in `dist/`.
{% if sources or embeddings %}
Validate each built component with `python3 scripts/validate_component.py source sources/<id>/source.wasm`
or `python3 scripts/validate_component.py embedding embeddings/<id>/embedding.wasm`, as applicable.
{% endif %}{% if sources %}Run `memcastle source test sources/<id>` to execute its conformance fixtures through the real host.
{% endif %}{% if embeddings %}Run each generated embedding probe against the actual archive:

```sh
python3 embeddings/<id>/tests/conformance.py --archive dist/{{ plugin_id }}-VERSION.tar.gz \
  --plugin-id {{ plugin_id }} --module-id <id>
```

This uses an isolated daemon to execute the sample provider and check the result through Core's embedding validation.
Adapt the sample model/profile in the helper when replacing the starter implementation.
{% endif %}

The package command reads `plugin.toml` and creates an archive with its own versioned `manifest.toml`
plus a matching `.sha256sum` file.
It does not rewrite `plugin.toml` or create a root-level `manifest.toml`.

A `VERSION` SemVer tag supplies a release version;
untagged Git commits get a development version.
Outside a Git checkout, pass `--version` when packaging.

## Project layout

| Path | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `plugin.toml` | Plugin identity, supported Core versions and module entries. |
{% if sources %}| `sources/<id>/` | Rust/Wasm source modules, each with its own manifest and tests. |
{% endif %}{% if integrations %}| `integrations/<id>/` | Agent integrations and their own assets or builds. |
{% endif %}{% if embeddings %}| `embeddings/<id>/` | Rust/Wasm embedding providers and model manifests. |
{% endif %}| `dist/` | Generated release archive and checksum after packaging. |

