{% endif %}
{% if gh_ship %}Releases use gh-ship and git-cliff:
merging a releasable Conventional Commit into `main` opens a `release/next` PR.
Merging the release PR publishes a validated `{{ plugin_id }}-VERSION.tar.gz` archive under the `VERSION` Git tag.

Configure the `release` environment with {% if ship_token == "app" %}variable `APP_CLIENT_ID`
and secret `APP_PRIVATE_KEY` for an App installed on this repository{% else %}secret `SHIP_TOKEN`
(fine-grained PAT){% endif %}.
The publish workflow uses this credential to check the draft release and upload its validated archive.
Grant contents, actions and pull requests write permission;
issues write is needed to create the release label.

Set squash-merge title to the PR title and body to blank, and enable the release environment.
The `prepare-release` workflow's `dry_run` input avoids pushing or committing.
{% else %}To publish, tag a reviewed commit on `main` as `VERSION`.
The release workflow rebuilds and validates the archive before publishing it;
it refuses an existing release.
{% endif %}
